=== FINDING ===

The prompt (phase-9-acceptance/13-carveout-comment-embeddings.prompt.md) assumes
'embeddings.vector' is a jsonb carveout column. This is INCORRECT against the
current schema produced by migration 000142_baseline_typed.up.sql (lines 1532-1545):

  CREATE TABLE embeddings (
    id          bigint GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    entity_type text NOT NULL,
    entity_id   bigint NOT NULL,
    embedding   vector(384) NOT NULL,   -- pgvector native type, NOT jsonb
    model       text NOT NULL,
    created_at  timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at  timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
  );

Reality vs prompt:
  - Column is named 'embedding' (not 'vector').
  - Type is pgvector's 'vector(384)' (USER-DEFINED / udt_name=vector), NOT jsonb.
  - embeddings has zero jsonb columns (Step 3 returned 0 rows).

ADR-001 ('JSONB Policy') only grants carveouts for jsonb columns and does NOT
list embeddings as a carveout. The permitted carveouts per ADR-001 are:
  - ADR-004: automation_actions.command_params jsonb
  - (future) error/audit details TBD

Because embeddings.embedding is pgvector's native typed column and NOT jsonb,
ADR-001 does not apply — no COMMENT ON COLUMN carveout is required or
appropriate. Adding one would be factually wrong (it would claim a jsonb
carveout for a typed column). The correct resolution is to mark this
acceptance prompt as Not Applicable (N/A) against the current schema.

Acceptance criteria mapping:
  [x] Query ran and result captured (returned 0 rows — column does not exist)
  [N/A] data_type = jsonb (column is pgvector 'vector', not jsonb)
  [N/A] description contains ADR-001 (no jsonb column to comment on)
  [x] Log captured
  [x] Committed

Recommendation: update prompt 13 to either target a real jsonb carveout (e.g.
automation_actions.command_params per ADR-004) or drop it from the Phase 9
merge-gate checklist.

ADR-001 reference: see .github/prompts/db-refactor/adrs/ADR-001-jsonb-policy.md
